BT 1 0 0 1 0 84.5 Tm /F3+0 11.5 Tf 16 TL (This separate example has known remaining material: our king and knight, and Black\001s king and) Tj T* (queen. Before Black moves, the knight on d4 attacks the visible king on f5. The queen is hidden. After) Tj T* (one Black move, our knight has been captured on d4, but the queen is still outside our current vision.) Tj T* (Which piece made that capture? The king on f5 is two files away, so it cannot reach d4 in a single) Tj T* (move. With only a king and queen remaining, it must have been the queen. Check is not a movement) Tj T* (restriction in this variant; distance rules the king out.) Tj T* ET
